+# Tracker2KSP v0.4.9 — native Impulse Tracker loader baseline
+
+Tracker2KSP now recognises and parses **native `IMPM` / `.it` modules** instead of treating “IT support” as only IT-authored S3M. Native IT has its own physically separate Z80 engine (`compact_engine_it.bin`) and its own parser/runtime profile; S3M, IT-S3M, XM and MOD remain isolated. No KSP 1.05 or KSP1PLAY 0.48 format change is required.
+
+## What v0.4.9 adds
+
+- Native IT header/order/parapointer parsing, including creator/compatible-version flags and 64-channel pan/volume state.
+- Native **IT packed-pattern masks**, including per-channel previous mask/note/instrument/volume/effect reuse and variable row counts.
+- Native sample headers with 8/16-bit and mono/stereo PCM conversion to the signed mono OPL4 sample path.
+- **IT 2.14 and 2.15 compressed samples** with adaptive bit-width decoding; IT 2.15 double-delta integration is handled separately.
+- Sample-mode playback and a deliberately conservative **simple instrument-mode** path with the 120-entry note/sample keymap. The first instrument-mode implementation accepts NNA=Cut, no DCT/DCA, no active envelopes, no pitch-pan/randomisation and no instrument default pan.
+- IT note cut/off handling for the supported no-envelope/NNA-Cut profile. In sample mode, Note Fade is correctly ignored; instrument-mode Note Fade remains fail-fast until fadeout/background-voice handling exists.
+- IT command-memory split: D/K/L share volume-slide memory; E/F share pitch-slide memory; G links to E/F only when the IT compatibility header flag requests it; H/I/R nibble memory and O offset memory are kept independently.
+- IT `Cxx` row break follows hexadecimal IT semantics (strict S3M remains BCD).
+- Native-IT realtime corrections are isolated in `compact_engine_it.asm`: Dxy uses IT's Dx0/D0x/DxF/DFx decision order, Hxy and Rxy use new-effects finer depth/every-tick stepping, Ixy uses exact x-on/y-off lengths, and Qx6 uses exact floor(2*volume/3) retrigger volume.
+- Native Sxx no longer leaks ST3 behavior: S1x/S2x are ignored, invalid S3x/S4x waveform values are ignored rather than masked, and SC0/SD0 use IT-compatible tick-1 behavior.
+- IT channel panning honours the song panning-separation byte. Saved disabled channels are omitted from the OPL4 voice map.
+- A fifth engine source/binary/map/list is built by `source/BUILD_ENGINES.py`: `compact_engine_it.*` (**8,926 bytes** in this release).
+- Added `CONVERT_IT_TO_KSP.py` and `tests/test_it_v049.py`.
+
+## Deliberately fail-fast in v0.4.9
+
+The parser refuses native IT features that would otherwise be rendered incorrectly by the current one-voice-per-channel engine. This includes NNA Continue/Note-Off/Note-Fade, DCT/DCA, enabled volume/pan/pitch envelopes, instrument-mode note fade/fadeout paths, instrument-only / instrument+special-note memory cases, empty instrument keymap sample slots, sustain/ping-pong loops, sample auto-vibrato, sample/instrument global-volume multipliers other than the neutral values, non-64 initial channel volume, enabled sample default panning, surround, IT Old Effects mode, linear E/F/G slides, Jxx arpeggio pending exact IT tick semantics, Txx tempo slides below 20h, and M/N/P/U/V/W/Y/Z runtime effects.
+
+This is intentional: v0.4.9 is the **real native-IT file/packing/sample foundation**, not a claim that full Impulse Tracker voice allocation and envelope semantics are complete. The next true-IT pass can now be implemented against a real parser and a dedicated engine instead of extending IT-S3M.
+
+## v0.4.9 validation
+
+- `tests/test_it_v049.py`: **9/9 native-IT groups PASS** (packed-mask reuse, IT214/IT215 compressed zero-delta decode, simple instrument keymap, native IT effect-memory and Sxx isolation rules, sample-mode Note Fade, fail-fast guards, engine-runtime quirks, and end-to-end KSP build through the dedicated IT engine).
+- `tests/test_mod_v048.py`: **8/8 PASS**.
+- `tests/test_xm_v046.py`: **10/10 PASS**.
+- `tests/test_xm_v047.py`: **4/4 PASS**.
+- `tests/test_s3m_v045.py`: **4/4 PASS**.
+- Native IT engine: **8,926 bytes**; ST3/S3M: 9,054; IT-S3M: 8,926; MOD: 10,674; XM: 6,472.
+
+## Usage
+
+```text
+python3 CONVERT_TRACKER_TO_KSP.py song.it
+python3 CONVERT_IT_TO_KSP.py song.it
+```
+
+---
+
 # Tracker2KSP v0.4.8 — generic MOD / ProTracker compatibility pass
 
 Tracker2KSP converts MOD, XM, S3M and IT-authored/modern S3M modules to compact realtime MoonSound/OPL4 KSP 1.05. v0.4.8 is a focused MOD/ProTracker pass on top of v0.4.7. The four tracker runtimes remain physically separate; no KSP format or KSP1PLAY change is required.
