+# Tracker2KSP v0.4.9 test report
+
+## Native IT baseline
+
+The v0.4.8 tree was used as the regression baseline. v0.4.9 adds a native `IMPM` parser and a physically separate native-IT engine without changing KSP 1.05. Unsupported true-IT runtime semantics are rejected rather than silently downgraded to IT-S3M behaviour.
+
+### Automated regressions
+
+```text
+pytest -q tests/test_it_v049.py
+PYTHONPATH=. python3 tests/test_mod_v048.py
+python3 tests/test_xm_v046.py
+python3 tests/test_xm_v047.py
+python3 tests/test_s3m_v045.py
+```
+
+Results: **9/9 IT**, **8/8 MOD**, **10/10 + 4/4 XM**, **4/4 S3M** PASS.
+
+### Engine build
+
+`python3 source/BUILD_ENGINES.py` builds five independent binaries:
+
+- ST3/S3M: 9,054 bytes
+- IT-authored/modern S3M: 8,926 bytes
+- native IT: 8,926 bytes
+- MOD: 10,674 bytes
+- XM: 6,472 bytes
+
+### End-to-end native IT smoke
+
+`CONVERT_IT_TO_KSP.py tests/native_it_smoke_v049.it` builds a KSP 1.05 file through the dedicated native-IT engine: **17,564 bytes**, **8,926-byte engine**, no converter warnings, SHA-256 `c3507828cdf9e555c857f36f1e9dd5dfe0613fe73b0b726271fd9552bcdeffe6`.
+
+### Native IT coverage
+
+Covered now: IMPM header/tables, IT packed pattern masks and reuse, sparse-to-dense channel mapping, IT 2.14/2.15 compressed sample decoding, uncompressed 8/16-bit mono/stereo PCM, simple NNA-Cut instrument keymaps, sample-mode Note Fade ignore semantics, IT hexadecimal Cxx, effect-memory separation, native Sxx isolation, IT D/H/I/R/Q realtime differences, and a dedicated native-IT engine.
+
+Still intentionally rejected pending native runtime work: background NNA voices/DCT/DCA, envelopes/fadeout, instrument-only/special-note memory cases, empty instrument keymap slots, channel/sample/instrument volume multipliers, sustain/ping-pong loops, auto-vibrato, sample default pan/surround, linear E/F/G, Old Effects, Jxx exact IT arpeggio timing, tempo slides and M/N/P/U/V/W/Y/Z.
+
